  "decision_conditions": [
    "The development hereby permitted must be begun not later than the end of three years from the date of this permission.  \r \rReason: To comply with the provisions of S.51 of the Planning & Compulsory Purchase Act 2004.\r",
    "The development hereby permitted shall be carried out in accordance with the following approved plans: \r\r3520/AE/07 Location Plan and Block Plan Dated July 2025;\r3520/AE/01 Rev A Existing Ground and First-Floor Plans Dated March 2025;\r3520/AE/02 Existing Front, Rear and Side Elevations Dated January 2025;\r3520/AE/03 Rev G Proposed Ground-Floor Plan Dated July 2026;\r3520/AE/04 Rev B Proposed First Floor Plan Dated July 2026;\r3520/AE/05 Rev E Proposed Front, Rear and Side Elevations Dated July 2026;\r3520/AE/06 Rev B Existing and Proposed Roof Layout Dated June 2026;\r3520/AE/08 Rev C Existing and Proposed Section A-A Dated June 2026;\r3520/AE/12 Construction of a single storey rear extension Dated 20 June 2026;\rDesign and Access Statement 3521/AE/DA Dated June 2026;\rHeritage Statement Ref. 3520/AE/HS Dated June 2026;\rArboricultural Method Statement Arbtech Dated 03 July 2025;\rArboricultural Impact Assessment Plan Arbtech AIA 01 Dated July 2025;\rTree Protection Plan\tArbtech TPP 01 Dated July 2025;\rEnvironment Agency Flood Map for Planning Dated 18 February 2025;\rSuDS Pro Forma;\t\rSustainable Urban Drainage Systems Management Plan 3521/AE/SuDS Dated June 2026;\rPermeable Paving Construction Detail and Maintenance Plan 3520/AE/PPC Dated June 2026;\rAgent email with clarifying amended drawings Dated 27 July 2026.\r\rReason: For the avoidance of doubt and in the interests of proper planning.\r",
    "All new external work shall be carried out in materials that resemble, as closely as possible, in colour and texture as specified in the approved application.\r\rReason: To safeguard the appearance of the premises and preserve the character of the conservation area.\r",
    "Prior to the commencement of construction works, details of how surface water from the proposed extension and associated hardstanding will be managed shall be submitted to and approved in writing by the Local Planning Authority. The details shall include the proposed drainage arrangements, any necessary attenuation or controlled discharge, and arrangements for future maintenance.\r\rThe approved drainage measures and permeable paving shall be installed before the extension is first brought into use and shall thereafter be retained and maintained in accordance with the approved details.\r\rReason: To ensure that surface-water runoff is appropriately managed and that the development does not increase flood risk on the site or elsewhere, in accordance with Policies DMD 59 and DMD 61 of the Enfield Development Management Document.\r"
  ],
